# DAX Measures

All measures are stored in a dedicated `_Measures` table, kept separate from the fact table for organization and reusability.

### Core Aggregations

Total Sales = SUM(Table_1[Sales])

Total Profit = SUM(Table_1[Profit])

Total Units Sold = SUM(Table_1[Units Sold])

Average Discount = AVERAGE(Table_1[Discounts])

### Profit Margin

Profit Margin = DIVIDE([Total Profit], [Total Sales])

Uses DIVIDE() instead of the / operator to safely return blank rather than an error on any zero-denominator edge case.

### Time Intelligence

Year-to-Date Sales = TOTALYTD([Total Sales], Calendar[Date])

Year-to-Date Profit = TOTALYTD([Total Profit], Calendar[Date])

Previous Year Profit = 
CALCULATE(
    [Total Profit], 
    SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR(Calendar[Date])
)

Growth Percentage = 
DIVIDE(
    [Total Profit] - [Previous Year Profit], 
    [Previous Year Profit]
)

Note: All three time intelligence measures reference Calendar[Date] — a dedicated date table — rather than the raw Table_1[Date] or Table_1[Year] column. 
Initial versions referencing the fact table's own Year column returned blank for Previous Year Profit, caused by a filter context conflict: 
the visual's Year filter and SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR's shifted date filter were both active simultaneously on different columns, producing zero matching rows.
Building a proper Date table, marking it as such, and relating it to the fact table resolved this — the standard, recommended pattern for time intelligence in Power BI.
